    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present No. 15 Cherrymount Park to the market.\n\nPositioned at the end of a peaceful cul-de-sac, this charming semi-detached home dates from the 1940s and enjoys a superb setting just off the North Circular Road, adjacent to the vibrant village of Phibsborough. Beautifully maintained over the years, the property offers a wonderful balance of character, comfort and practicality. Many original features have been carefully preserved, including tiled fireplaces and polished wooden floors. The house is filled with natural light and benefits from well-proportioned living spaces, creating a welcoming atmosphere from the moment you step inside. A particular feature of the property is its impressive outdoor space. The front garden provides valuable off-street parking and the landscaped rear garden featuring a pergola structure, outdoor lighting, dedicated seating area with firepit and a MoonBoard climbing wall, with the added benefit of side access.\n\nPresented in excellent condition throughout, the accommodation is both spacious and well laid out. The entrance hall features engineered Junkers flooring, ceiling covings, ample storage and a useful guest w.c. To the front of the property is an elegant living room with wood burning stove as a focal point, original pocket doors open through to the second reception room which overlooks the rear garden with glass double doors providing direct access to the garden. The kitchen/ dining room is located off the hallway with the dining area finished with decorative wood paneling and a large window overlooking the garden. The kitchen is fitted with a range of floor and wall units with open shelving and a cleverly concealed pantry hidden behind timber paneling. A door leads to the rear garden. The garage can also be accessed internally from the hallway and is currently used as a gym/ utility area with plumbing for a washing machine.\n\nUpstairs off the landing there are four spacious bedrooms and a very stylish shower room with high-quality fixtures and fittings. \n\nThe property enjoys an desirable location just off the North Circular Road, within easy walking distance of both Phibsborough and Stoneybatter, two of Dublin 7's most popular neighbourhoods. Residents are spoiled for choice with an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, bars and local amenities all close by. The area is particularly well served by educational facilities, with a number of primary and secondary schools nearby, while TU Dublin's Grangegorman campus is just a short walk from the property. Dublin City Centre is easily accessible on foot, making this an ideal location for those seeking a convenient urban lifestyle.\n\nTransport links are excellent, with numerous Dublin Bus routes servicing the area, while the Luas Green Line is just a few minutes' walk away. The Phoenix Park and National Botanic Gardens and Royal Canal Greenway are within easy reach, offering an abundance of outdoor and recreational amenities. A number of key city destinations, including the Four Courts, Blackhall Place and the Mater Hospital, are also located nearby."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHallway - \nBright entrance hall with engineered Junkers flooring, recessed lighting, under-stairs storage, and additional storage within an alcove space.\n\nLiving Room - \nThis is a beautiful reception room to the front of the house with a wood burning stove creating a lovely focal point, other features include engineered Junkers flooring, ceiling covings and pocket doors to the second reception room.\n\nReception Room - \nAnother generous sized reception room with a tiled fireplace and double glass doors opening onto the rear garden.\n\nDining Room - \nWith decorative wooden paneling, vertical radiators and a sliding pocket door.\n\nKitchen - \nFitted with a great range of high-quality modern floor and wall units with open shelving, fisher Paykel fridge freezer, fisher Paykel double drawer dishwasher and smeg oven. The floor and splashback are laid in ceramic tiles and there is the benefit of a pantry.\n\nWC - \nWith ceramic tiled flooring, w.c and wash hand basin.\n\nGarage - \nPositioned to the side of the property, the garage is currently in use as a gym/ utility space with plumbing for a washing machine and features a timber door, concrete floor, and excellent storage space with a new roof and skylight.\n\nLanding - \nRecessed lighting and provides access to attic.\n\nBedroom Four/Office - \nWith original wooden flooring.\n\nShower Room - \nFully tiled and comprising a shower, w.c, wash hand basin, and bidet.\n\nBedroom One - \nPositioned to the front of the property, a spacious double bedroom laid with solid oak flooring.\n\nBedroom Two - \nPositioned to the rear of the property, this double bedroom features built-in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom Three - \nWith laminate flooring and Philips Hue smart lighting. This is an acoustically treated room with Rockwool acoustic insulation on the floor and ceilings as well as soundproof ecoboard.\n\nGarden - \nBeautifully landscaped rear garden featuring a pergola structure, outdoor lighting, dedicated seating area with firepit and a MoonBoard climbing wall. The garden is further enhanced by a variety of mature and newly planted trees.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Beautifully decorated and presented 1940's family home</li><li>Peaceful cul de sac location</li><li>Period features throughout</li><li>Replumbed with new three-zone combi boiler</li><li>New Carlson AluClad windows and doors</li><li>Renovated kitchen and shower room with underfloor heating</li><li>Landscaped rear garden with pergola and firepit</li><li>Electric vehicle charging point</li><li>Acoustically treated music room</li><li>Cat 6 cable wiring/comms hub</ul>"
      },
